{"title":"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Each of eight boxes contains six balls. Each ball has been colored with one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> colors, such that no two balls in the same box are the same color, and no two colors occur together in more than one box. Determine, with justification, the smallest integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> for which this is possible. \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We claim that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/2/0626c3401dd2b0192afc70c8825027494215207a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=23$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is the minimum. Consider the following construction (replacing colors with numbers) which fulfills this:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/7/f77c8aaf0c50d3db98fe5556770b8d432abc5752.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left[ \\begin{array}{cccccccc} 1 &amp; 1 &amp; 1 &amp; 2 &amp; 3 &amp; 4 &amp; 5 &amp; 6 \\\\ 2 &amp; 7 &amp; 12 &amp; 7 &amp; 8 &amp; 9 &amp; 10 &amp; 11 \\\\ 3 &amp; 8 &amp; 13 &amp; 12 &amp; 13 &amp; 14 &amp; 15 &amp; 16 \\\\ 4 &amp; 9 &amp; 14 &amp; 17 &amp; 17 &amp; 17 &amp; 18 &amp; 19 \\\\ 5 &amp; 10 &amp; 15 &amp; 18 &amp; 20 &amp; 22 &amp; 20 &amp; 21 \\\\ 6 &amp; 11 &amp; 16 &amp; 19 &amp; 21 &amp; 23 &amp; 22 &amp; 23 \\end{array} \\right]\\]\" width=\"282\" height=\"117\" />\nSuppose a configuration exists with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/9/309ea8a480044fd0b257cc363f1e565c25e77479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\le 22$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p>Suppose a ball appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or more times. Then the remaining balls of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes must be distinct, so that there are at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/1/971bbcf932d0d97f4ce6af76013a2d90097acf44.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 5 \\cdot 5 + 1 = 26$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"139\" height=\"15\" /> balls, contradiction. If a ball appears <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> or more times, the remaining balls of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes must be distinct, leading to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/0/7300038c4aac2fcdac970a4e22d10c7ee2c450dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\cdot 4 + 1 = 21$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"104\" height=\"14\" /> balls. The fifth box can contain at most four balls from the previous boxes, and then the remaining two balls must be distinct, leading to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/c/50c562a13c56595eba74034319f6a804b281e73b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 2 + 21 = 23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"126\" height=\"15\" />, contradiction.\n</p><p>However, by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Pigeonhole_Principle\" title=\"Pigeonhole Principle\">Pigeonhole Principle</a>, at least one ball must appear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a> suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> appears three times, and let the boxes that contain these have balls with colors <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/e/08e1f3b58d32b5554da4bc53ef63651310970973.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\{1,2,3,4,5,6\\},\\{1,7,8,9,10,11\\},\\{1,12,13,14,15,16\\}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"418\" height=\"18\" />. Each of the remaining five boxes can have at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> balls from each of these boxes. Thus, each of the remaining five boxes must have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> additional balls <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/f/31f840d75e1ae20831f06fed8e19cb57cc4e2e6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$&gt; 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. Thus, it is necessary that we use <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/6/f96d65393dc63692baeda603e97ac1226f6620e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\le 22 - 16 = 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"110\" height=\"15\" /> balls to fill a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/c/83cc3f3015106f232a58f1ad3fd29d868ef9e1dc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" /> grid by the same rules. \n</p><p>Again, no balls may appear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/5/a152e411b6d6031f429c54be88920f1e56c2da2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\ge 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"30\" height=\"16\" /> times, but by Pigeonhole, one ball must appear <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times. <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Without_loss_of_generality\" title=\"Without loss of generality\">Without loss of generality</a>, let this ball have color <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />; then the three boxes containing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/6/b7616a230c77f0d9a577e5bca01aa06f1c35c457.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$17$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> must have at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/a/17a27be20cf44de385dff1637cb85c5ea8bde986.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3 + 1 = 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"96\" height=\"14\" /> balls, contradiction.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087272e81dcb5b0c76bb0aa6b4cd9c24a6cdf749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 23$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is the minimum.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to the above solution, no color can appear 4 times or more.\n</p><p>We can use PIE. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/6/ab6fbd120703f8e89b70020fbe8a15fd78cf69e3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_1,S_2,\\cdots ,S_8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"109\" height=\"18\" /> be the colors in each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/5/8455f3b5cb3b4880b8c9d782a5c1f0334db819eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> boxes. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2c9737608c9df6befdd17786f5df258c216a67.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=|\\cup_{i=1}^8S_i|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"102\" height=\"19\" />. By PIE we know that<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/b/dbbb4199498e41312da429d12229f0dd8c9ef3d8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\cup_{i=1}^8S_i|=\\sum_{i=1}^8 |S_i|-\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j|+\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j&lt;k\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j\\cap S_k|-\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j&lt;k&lt;l\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j\\cap S_k\\cap S_l|\\cdots.\\]\" width=\"702\" height=\"53\" />Note however that no color can appear 4 times or more, so all the items after <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/a/d2a6b746300f71e8a36f690ef1d80fb2f706eea5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j&lt;k\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j\\cap S_k|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"178\" height=\"40\" /> must be equal to 0, so<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/3/7e3b32b4b3cfebcc0a529c31b435bfd41725292c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|\\cup_{i=1}^8S_i|=\\sum_{i=1}^8 |S_i|-\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j|+\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j&lt;k\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j\\cap S_k|.\\]\" width=\"476\" height=\"53\" />Now note that for each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b52777ff0f61a3a3099bea80c124f6a457559cea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|S_i|=6,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"64\" height=\"18\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/6/c46ab718c5ff7f5ab1223185fecafab16e6befe5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{i=1}^8 |S_i|=48.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -20px\" width=\"101\" height=\"50\" /> Also no pair of colors appears twice, so for any <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/2/a7223f3c531adcb97e6199644823cbdfdcca3988.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i,j, |S_i\\cap S_j|\\leq 1,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"135\" height=\"20\" /> and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/2/1421b4e17130fb45f2bfdc4b58347d017211e9c3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j|\\leq \\binom82=28.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"230\" height=\"54\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/c/81c7924e2b1bb037e8f0813a6113b146c4cd7432.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 48-28+\\sum_{1\\leq i&lt;j&lt;k\\leq 8}|S_i\\cap S_j\\cap S_k|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"300\" height=\"40\" /> Given that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> colors, to minimize the number of colors in 3 boxes means each color is in either 2 or 3 boxes, and since there are 48 total spots, this means there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/0/00095334ce7141d38ae7a326c6b22747641bf7f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$48-2n$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> colors in 3 boxes and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/b/18bea8de4cc26d0a81ceff02aa40880bda76d639.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n-48$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> colors in 2. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/7/66743034b318b935765ea108568f41db9530c2d1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq 20+48-2n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"140\" height=\"16\" /> so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/c/a7c02703ff8bbd71e0232794d2440c6a8f08943f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3n\\geq 68$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"64\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/2/e3227957db7896dd3edafd001225e5b3d70f7169.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\geq23$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" /> and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c08c2206b21fad268f42394ca736f22a4734b6ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{i,j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> be the number of balls which are the same color as the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/8/ec8eb9058cb3a532b3b4a1f33e169e8421c22a3d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$j^{\\text{th}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"21\" height=\"19\" /> ball in box <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" /> (including that ball). For a fixed box <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa5c0f2ff240388cff3aa67b700aaaedd436b6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\leq i\\leq 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"72\" height=\"15\" />, consider the sums\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/c/5fced613b1f4375005c6b01213dda8974ddb0325.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[S_i = \\sum_{j=1}^6 m_{i,j}\\quad\\text{and}\\quad s_i = \\sum_{j=1}^6 \\frac{1}{m_{i,j}}.\\]\" width=\"267\" height=\"52\" />\nFor each fixed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/8/34857b3ba74ce5cd8607f3ebd23e9015908ada71.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"14\" />, since no pair of colors is repeated, each of the remaining seven boxes can contribute at most one ball to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/0/9e0ec34cd8860ceb97113f81ba768ba739ad5166.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/9/b3951c853ccf39ccd213b78ce024f2970acc860c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S_i\\leq 13$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"58\" height=\"15\" />. It follows by the convexity of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/c/39cec31af9b5c2259b9c1ece85f6670feb4f2e58.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(x) = 1/x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"87\" height=\"18\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b63c17213f84d730e0de1f8c08597f7a648e37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is minimized when one of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/8/c08c2206b21fad268f42394ca736f22a4734b6ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m_{i,j}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"30\" height=\"12\" /> is equal to 3 and the other five equal to 2. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/d/85d8fb67e4ed1cd814a453cdeed1d265e0821bbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$s_i\\geq 17/6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"74\" height=\"18\" />. Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/e/e/7ee023cd1f479cf78c65d9f2a98aeb62627b5c1f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[n = \\sum_{i=1}^8 \\sum_{j=1}^6 \\frac{1}{m_{i,j}}\\geq 8\\cdot\\frac{17}{6} = \\frac{68}{3}.\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"52\" />\nHence there must be 23 colors. The construction for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/7/087272e81dcb5b0c76bb0aa6b4cd9c24a6cdf749.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 23$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" /> is above.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:40%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO\" title=\"2001 USAMO\">2001 USAMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=27&amp;year=2001\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_USAMO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 USAMO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=USAMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"USAMO Problems and Solutions\"> All USAMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div 